oder to develop properly.\n\nNow I'm organizing all the experiments into the YAML format, making sure to include plan_019 which is still running alongside the planned experiments from plan_020 through plan_025, and filtering out the ones that already have final evaluation results. I've got all four seeds evaluated for the depth experiments with their CAR and TSR metrics, so I can calculate the aggregate means — CAR averaging around 0.780 and TSR around 0.889 across the seeds.\n\nNow I'm looking at the results for the cutoff and vanilla approaches. The vanilla 3-seed results are complete with a mean CAR of 0.780 and TSR of 0.907, while cutoff still has one seed running. I'm also starting to compile the detach 3-seed results. Cohen's d comes out to 3.95, which puts it solidly in the best tier range. Now I'm thinking through what tables and figures each experiment needs—for the cutoff work, I need a dose-response curve showing how performance changes across cutoff steps, and for the gradient tracking experiment, I'll want to visualize the per-layer gradient norms as they evolve during training. The second benchmark will require the full set of results across all conditions.\n\nI also need to include predictions for plan_019 even though it's still running, and I'm working out the target ranges for the 3-seed cutoff scenario in the best tier case.\n\nWriting YAML output... Now I'm looking at the per-task predictions for cutoff_s2 by examining how each task performed across s0 and s1. Most tasks show stable performance, but T3 is notably volatile with a jump from 0.58 to 0.74, so I'm predicting it'll drop back down to 0.50 given that high variance pattern. I need to fine-tune these predictions to get closer to 0.789. Adjusting T3 up to 0.56 and T6 to 0.48 gives me a mean of 0.788, which is close enough. Now I'm looking at the TSR values, starting with T0 and T1.\n\nFor the remaining TSR entries, I'm setting T2 through T9 to hit a target mean around 0.910. Tweaking T5 from